{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Tips on IT Procurement: What the Company Is Paying for"}, {"type": "position", "content": 11}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 3}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about prices for IT Procurement."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understand information about people's backgrounds in spoken or written documents.  Participate in the improvement of IT contracts, establishing technical clauses that respond to the needs of the negotiating agents, based on current laws on contracting."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of a range of grammar and vocabulary, and with the appropriate level of formality and purpose, coherence and cohesion for the context.  Recognizes simple ideas on concepts on IT contracts and knowledge transfer, simulated processes of IT contracting, and technological negotiation."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n7le03ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Passive of Modal Verbs Must and Have to "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When we don't know who the doer of an action is or it is not important, we use the <span class=\"strong\">passive voice</span>; the importance is given to the object of the sentence.  "}, {"type": "text", "content": "We use the modals <span class=\"strong\">must be</span> or <span class=\"strong\">have to be</span> + a verb in <span class=\"strong\">past participle</span> to talk about obligations. <span class=\"strong\">Passive voice</span> is used when the focus is on the action and the object of the sentence. Let's take a look at the grammatical structure: <br/><br/>  </span>Object + <span class=\"strong\">Must be</span> / <span class=\"strong\">Have to be</span> + <span class=\"strong\">Verb in Past Participle</span> + Complement</div><br/><br/>  Examples: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">Rates <span class=\"strong\">must be established</span> from the beginning. </span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">Rates <span class=\"strong\">have to be agreed</span> upon. </span><br/><br/>   Mentioning who does the action is optional. If you want to mention the doer, you need to use the preposition <span class=\"strong\">by</span>. Let's see an example: <br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">Rates <span class=\"strong\">have to be agreed</span> upon <span class=\"strong\">by</span> the customer and the company. </span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Conditions must be set clear to reduce the possibility of having fees changed."}, {"type": "example", "content": "What has been economically agreed has to be clearly expressed, so rates will not change unexpectedly causing us trouble. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Of course, all taxes other than GST, or Good and Services Tax, have to be included in the fee."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "at will"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "any time you want "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Sometimes, supplier contracts often make reference to the supplier's \u201cthen current rate\u201d or allow the supplier to change their rates regularly, which give them the power to vary prices at will.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le03ob11aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "fee model"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a framework for generating revenues"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Since price drives behavior, I think we're going to have to find some good commercial advice so we can come up with a good fee model."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le03ob11aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "GST"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "stands for Goods and Services Tax; a tax levied when a consumer buys a good or service"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(abbreviation)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Of course, all taxes other than GST, or Good and Services Tax, have to be included in the fee ."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le03ob11aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "peripheral"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "device used to put in and extract information from a computer "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Apart from desktop software, operating systems, we're going to offer computer hardware and peripherals, right? "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le03ob11aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "current rate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "current price available for a good or service"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Sometimes, supplier contracts often make reference to the supplier's \u201cthen current rate\u201d or allow the supplier to change their rates regularly, which give them the power to vary prices at will.   "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le03ob11aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "value-added"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "gross income"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Well, not everything can become a \u2018value-added' consulting service which is required on a time basis."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le03ob11aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Questions within Questions "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Questions within questions</span> or <span class=\"strong\">embedded questions</span> are a way to ask questions in a very polite way. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Sometimes there is a <span class=\"strong\">question</span> that is <span class=\"strong\">embedded</span> or included within another question. This kind of structure is used to ask for further information or to ask for something indirectly. In this kind of questions, the first part of the questions is a direct question that usually starts with any of the following expressions: <br/>  <ul><li>Could you tell me\u2026? </li> <li>Do you know\u2026? </li> <li>Can you remember\u2026?</li></ul>  The second part of this type of questions refers to the actual information we want to ask about. It starts with a <span class=\"strong\">WH Question</span> when it is an open question or with <span class=\"strong\">If</span> or <span class=\"strong\">Whether</span> when the question has a Yes/No answer and it is followed by a regular affirmative sentence. <br/><br/>  Example: <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Could you tell me</span> what the price of the software is? </span> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Do you know</span> if that software is expensive? </span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "But, can you tell me about the prices we're going to offer our clients?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Can you tell me if we plan to change the rates periodically?"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for information about IT procurement for contracts"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Describe the most important tips to be taken into account when making a supplies contract."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a poster explaining your tips"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Present the poster to your partners"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": 